{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Third plan review 2026-10-18 (BLOCK, 3 moves). All three verified on origin/main b97d414b8e2 and fixed in the description; the line inventories that no longer fit the 8,000-char description cap live here.\n\n1. `check` delegation and handler signatures. `check_ac_cli(argv, tracker)` (`_engine_support/gates.py:82`) and `quality_check_cli(argv, tracker)` (`:388`) are 2-arg; `clarity_check_cli(argv, tracker, repo_root)` (`:211`) is 3-arg; the `argv_tracker_root` adapter calls `fn(rest, tracker, None)` (`_execute.py:122`). Resolution: the new `check_cli(argv, tracker, repo_root)` is the single 3-arg entry the adapter calls; it parses `--ac|--clarity|(default)` and calls each handler with its CURRENT signature. No handler changes signature. New AC: the three `main([\"check\", ...])` forms exit 0/1 with no `TypeError`.\n\n2. `list --limit` default. `build_list` has no `--limit` today (`_parsers/core/reads.py`); the old `session-logs` verb defaulted to 5 (`reads_cli.py:363`). Resolution: `list` gains `--limit N` (positive int), absent means all rows (list's current behaviour); the removed-spelling hint names `list --type=session_log --limit=5` so the old default is reachable by copy-paste. New AC covers no-limit, `--limit=2`, and `--limit=0` (exit 2).\n\n3. CI-run tests still driving removed verbs (beyond the registry/dispatch tests already listed):\n   - `tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py:51,55,76,77` census rows for `exists`, `clarity-check`, `tag`, `untag`; `:150,154` parametrize rows `(\"exists\", [\"some-ticket\"])`, `(\"tag\", [\"some-ticket\",\"atag\"])`.\n   - `tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py:135,142,150,152,157,159` subprocess `_cli(\"tag\"|\"untag\", ...)` cases; `:528` `_confirm.leaf_confirm(\"tag\", ...)`.\n   - `tests/unit/test_cli_body_guard.py:160,165,170` `commands_main([\"tag\"|\"untag\", ...])`.\n   - `tests/fixtures/ticket-cli-baseline.json:31,37` `tag`/`untag` entries.\n   All retarget to `edit --add-tag/--remove-tag` or `check`. The repo-wide grep for the 12 removed spellings also hits non-verb string literals (`\"format\"`, `\"exists\"` as dict keys in unrelated tests, `mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`, `api_surface_baseline.json`); those are judged per hit and left alone. The post-edit grep output is to be pasted into a comment.\n\nRegistry/docs line cites moved out of the description (all on b97d414b8e2): delete routes at `_registry.py:106,108-109,110-117,113,135-136` and `:200-280,388-390`; `docs/exit-codes.md` rows `:132,134,142,143,148,149,153,155,168,171,194`; `docs/user-guide.md:30,32,239,240,251,266,297,306-308`; `gen_cli_reference.py` `MUTATION_VERBS:125-136`, `EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE:47-49`; `scripts/probe_rebar.py:333-341,418-424,435,441,471-478,490,511-516`; `test_cli_registry_dispatch.py:168-196,459`; `test_cross_session_warn_routes.py:24-41`; `test_cli_registry.py:_CENSUS_SETS:29-47`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792370087067565090,"uuid":"2cf127ea-ce3e-4fc7-ba0d-c9e5f2806719"}